	(text "Peeple Beeper PCB. One cell. USB 5 V feeds the charger only. The buck makes 3.3 V for the ESP32, radio, screen, GPS switch, compass, backlight, motor, and piezo.\nLeave IO0, IO45, and IO46 open. IO3 has a pulldown so USB programming stays selected.\nGPS VCC and V_BCKP are the switched rail, with 4.7 \u00b5F, 100 nF, and 33 pF to ground. The 33 pF sits closest to the module. A low on the enable pin turns the module on. RESET_N is open-drain, with no pull-up.\nIO38 reaches GPS RXD through 1 k\\u03a9, with 5.6 k\\u03a9 to ground, so the pin stays under its 3.1 V high.\nThe backlight is a low-side switch on LCD_BLK, and BLA is 3.3 V. Screen V0, XV0, and VG stay open. Radio DIO2 stays open; it steers the antenna switch inside the module."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 250 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
